// @@@ The result of the nextSetBit method is either -1 or a value that is greater or equal to the fromIndex.

--------------------
// @@@ For any non-negative starting index fromIndex, the result of nextSetBit(fromIndex) is -1 if there is no set bit after fromIndex, or it is a non-negative number that is greater or equal to fromIndex.

--------------------
// @@@ If the starting index for searching for a set bit is negative, the result should be -1, indicating that there are no such bits. If the starting index is non-negative, the result should be either -1 (indicating no set bit found after the starting index) or a non-negative integer that is greater or equal to the starting index (indicating the index of the first set bit found after the starting index).

